$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ortho-borylation of 3,4-dimethoxybenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton
microreactor was charged with 3,4-dimethoxybenzaldehyde (1r) (166.1 mg,
1.0 mmol), t BuNH2 (420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL)
and stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried
under reduced pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), L1 (9.0 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25
μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M).
The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into
pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for
12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as
eluent). 245.0 mg of ortho-borylated benzaldehyde 2r (84%) as colourless
sticky liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.59 (s, 1H), 7.55 (s, 1H),
7.35 (s, 1H), 4.00 (s, 3H), 3.96 (s, 3H), 1.37 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 193.9, 152.9, 151.3, 136.4, 117.3, 108.7, 84.5, 56.3,
56.1, 25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 33.1. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C15H21BO5 [M+H]+ 293.1560, found 293.1553.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Ir-Catalyzed Ligand-Enabled Ortho and Meta Borylation of Aromatic
Aldehydes via in Situ-Generated Imines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bisht, Ranjana; Chattopadhyay, Buddhadeb
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2016), 138(1), 84-87

