$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ortho-borylation of 2-methoxybenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor
was charged with 2-methoxybenzaldehyde (1n) (136.1 mg, 1.0 mmol), t BuNH2
(420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h
at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure.
In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0
mg, 1.5 mol%), L1 (9.0 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2
(177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The microreactor was
capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into pre-heated aluminum
block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h. After
completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced pressure and
chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as eluent). 210.0
mg of ortho-borylated benzaldehyde 2n (80%) as sticky liquid. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.43 (s, 1H), 7.51 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.2
Hz, 1H), 6.96 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 1.43 (s, 12H). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 190.9, 161.6, 135.5, 128.2, 124.5, 112.3, 84.1, 55.7,
25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 32.8. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C14H19BO4 [M+Na]+ 285.1274, found 285.1263.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Ir-Catalyzed Ligand-Enabled Ortho and Meta Borylation of Aromatic
Aldehydes via in Situ-Generated Imines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bisht, Ranjana; Chattopadhyay, Buddhadeb
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2016), 138(1), 84-87

