$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 4-hydroxybenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor
was charged with 4-hydroxybenzaldehyde (122.1 mg, 1.0 mmol), MeNH2 (10.0
equiv) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h at room
temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure. In a
glove box, this crude imine was charged with HBpin (159.6 μL, 1.1
equiv.), [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%),
B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv.) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The
microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into
pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for
12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (5%
ethylacetate/hexane as eluent). 196.0 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde
3g (79%) as sticky liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.87 (s, 1H), 8.38
(s, 1H), 8.14 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.93 (dd, J = 8.4 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H),
6.98 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 1.39 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
190.9, 168.9, 140.5, 134.4, 129.3, 116.8, 85.3, 25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 33.3. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C13H17BO4 [M+H]+ 249.1220, found
249.1227.
