$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 2-borylatedbenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor
was charged with 2-borylatedbenzaldehyde (232.1 mg, 1.0 mmol), MeNH2
(10.0 equiv.) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h at
room temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure. In
a glove box, this crude imine was charged with [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg,
1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2
(177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The microreactor was
capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into pre-heated aluminum
block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h. After
completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced pressure and
chromatographic separation with silica gel (15% ethylacetate/hexane as
eluent). 276.0 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde 3m (77%) as gummy
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.42 (s, 1H), 8.33 (s, 1H), 7.97 (d,
J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.76 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 1.39 (s, 12H), 1.34 (s, 12H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 194.7, 140.3, 139.2, 135.3, 134.3, 83.2,
24.9, 24.6. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 34.0. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C19H28B2O5 [M+H]+ 359.2129, found 359.2129.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
