$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ortho-borylation of 4-carbomethoxybenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton
microreactor was charged with 4-carbomethoxybenzaldehyde (1f) (164.1 mg,
1.0 mmol), t BuNH2 (420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL)
and stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried
under reduced pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), 8-AQ (4.32 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin
(7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL,
0.4M). The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed
into pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred
for 12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as
eluent). 214.6 mg of ortho-borylated benzaldehyde 2f (74%) as solid. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.62 (s, 1H), 8.51 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 8.19
(dd, J = 8.4 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 8.01 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 3.96 (s, 3H),
1.40 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 194.3, 166.4, 144.3, 136.9,
133.7, 131.9, 127.8, 84.9, 52.6, 25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 33.6.
HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C15H19BO5 [M+H]+ 291.1404, found 291.1401.
