$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ortho-borylation of 3-fluorobenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor
was charged with 3-fluorobenzaldehyde (1k) (124.1 mg, 1.0 mmol), t BuNH2
(420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h
at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure.
In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0
mg, 1.5 mol%), 8-AQ (4.32 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%),
B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The microreactor
was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into pre-heated aluminum
block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h. After
completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced pressure and
chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as eluent). 180.0
mg of ortho-borylated benzaldehyde 2k (72%) as colourless liquid. Crude
GC/MS analysis showed that the ratios between two ortho isomers are:
75/25. During isolation, it underwent rapid protodeborylation. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.62 (d, JH-F = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (q, J = 6.0 Hz,
1H), 7.64 (dd, J = 9.2 Hz, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 7.27 (dt, J = 8.0 Hz, J = 2.4
Hz, 1H), 1.37 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 193.7, 164.8 (d, JC-F
= 251.3 Hz), 144.2 (d, JC-F = 6.3 Hz), 138.6 (d, JC-F = 7.6 Hz), 120.1
(d, JC-F = 20.6 Hz), 113.7 (d, JC-F = 21.3 Hz), 84.7, 25.0. 11B NMR (128
MHz, CDCl3): δ 31.3. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C13H16BFO3 [M+Na]+
273.1074, found 273.1063.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Ir-Catalyzed Ligand-Enabled Ortho and Meta Borylation of Aromatic
Aldehydes via in Situ-Generated Imines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bisht, Ranjana; Chattopadhyay, Buddhadeb
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2016), 138(1), 84-87

