$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 2-methylbenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor was
charged with 2-methylbenzaldehyde (120.0 mg, 1.0 mmol), MeNH2 (10.0
equiv.) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h at room
temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure. In a
glove box, this crude imine was charged with [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg,
1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2
(177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The microreactor was
capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into pre-heated aluminum
block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h. After
completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced pressure and
chromatographic separation with silica gel (2% ethylacetate/hexane as
eluent). 175.0 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde 3l (71%) as sticky
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.24 (s, 1H), 8.22 (s, 1H), 7.88 (d,
J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.27 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 2.66 (s, 3H), 1.36 (s, 12H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 193.7, 143.8, 140.2, 139.8, 133.8, 131.5,
84.3, 25.2, 20.5. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 33.3. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd
for C14H19BO3 [M+H]+ 247.1427, found 247.1426.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
