$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Meta-borylation of 4-chlorobenzaldehyde: A 5.0
mL Weaton microreactor was charged with 4-chlorobenzaldehyde (1b) (140.5
mg, 1.0 mmol), t BuNH2 (420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0
mL) and stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried
under reduced pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25
μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M).
The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into
pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for
12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as
eluent) 202.0 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde 3b (76%) as sticky
liquid. Crude reaction mixture showed the meta/ortho ratio was 81/19 (GC
ratio). The same procedure was followed using methylamine instead (10.0
equiv.) instead of tert-butylamine and the outcomes are as follows:
Selectivity: meta/ortho = 100/0; Isolated yield: 70%. meta-borylated
benzaldehyde 3c. 1H NMR (800 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.89 (s, 1H), 8.20 (s, 1H),
7.95 (dd, J = 8.8 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 6.96 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 3.92 (s,
3H), 1.36 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 191.2, 169.0, 140.1,
134.2, 129.4, 110.6, 84.1, 56.2, 24.9. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 31.1.
HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C14H19BO4 [M+H]+ 263.1455, found 263.1445.
